From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bpereira <bpereira@cloudflare.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 22:05:40 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Compact node storage and retained layout state

Compact retained DOM node storage: image layers with no url keep no image storage,
and shadow-root data, comment contents, template and shadow-root links,
pseudo-element links, anonymous blocks, list-item data, transforms and the wide
special element payloads live in boxed side storage; table cell and row lists,
parser growth slack, inline-layout text and node-range slack are shrunk once built;
class atoms are a ThinVec; an element stores its namespace as a byte next to its
local name and an attribute its prefix and namespace apart from its local name;
element state, selector flags and boolean flags are packed; nullable node ids keep
NodeId alignment; the opaque-id side table keeps only slot versions; and element
layout state and inline text layouts are allocated on first use. Readers go through
accessors. Layout, paint and serialization output are unchanged.

Drop box state under subtrees that become display:none: release their inline
layouts, layout output, child lists and anonymous blocks when damage propagation
sees the root restyled to display:none, and rebuild them when the subtree is shown
again. getComputedStyle still reports elements in such a subtree by resolving their
style on demand, inside the layout thread state.

Evict the shaped text of inline roots far from the viewport: after each resolve,
inline roots more than two viewport heights away drop their shaped layout, which
TextLayout::layout rebuilds from the DOM, the saved inline box sizes and indent,
and the last line break. An evicted root keeps a compact 48-byte break summary so
layout can rebreak and measure it and lay out its absolutely positioned boxes,
pre-wrap text and top/bottom aligned spans without reshaping; recently laid out and
near-viewport roots, the last 256 roots a pass broke and roots read since the last
scan stay shaped. Text eviction is on by default. Layout, geometry and paint output
are unchanged.

Keep derived child lists only on box nodes: text, comment and shadow-root nodes
never own layout or paint child lists, so those borrowed lists live in storage only
box nodes allocate. On wasm32 Node shrinks from 68 to 52 bytes and its slot from 72
to 56.
